WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Read the silhouette. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Separate visible evidence from interpretation

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: A silhouette is observable evidence; words such as elegant or aggressive are interpretations. Start with lines, masses and spacing you can point to.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Observation: “the roofline slopes toward the rear.” Interpretation: “the shape looks fast.” Keep those claims separate.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Observation sort

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: A view supports interpretation; it cannot prove hidden structure or compliance alone.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Separate visible evidence from interpretation
